<title>TURKEY: Turkish trade gap rises 55 pct to $1.13 bln in Feb.</title>
<headline>Turkish trade gap rises 55 pct to $1.13 bln in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's trade deficit rose by 55 percent to $1.13 billion in February from $730 million in the same 1995 month, the State Institute of Statistics said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>It said exports rose by 7.9 percent to $1.67 billion in February from $1.55 billion in the same 1995 month and imports by 22.7 percent to $2.8 billion from $2.28 billion.</p>
<p>Officials said the figures were delayed due to &quot;technical difficulties&quot; arising from Turkey's customs union with the European Union which took effect on January 1, 1996.  </p>
<p>(Figures in bln dollars)</p>
<p>			Feb96   Feb95   Jan96   Jan-Feb96   Jan-Feb95</p>
<p>Exports FOB	 1.67    1.55    1.73	3.40	  3.09</p>
<p>Imports CIF	 2.80    2.28    3.02	5.82	  4.38</p>
<p>Trade balance    -1.13   -0.73   -1.13     -2.42	 -1.29</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
